@startuml stream-reveal
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam wrapWidth 200
title How an answer appears in chat-node\n(char/s or word/s, optional pacing after the LLM finishes)

actor User
participant "Chat page\n(sends the prompt)" as UI
participant "LlmService\nstreamAnswer()" as LLM
participant "Hidden buffers\naccContent / committed" as BUF
participant "rAF pump\ntick() / kickPump()" as PUMP
participant "ChatService\nnodes() signal" as SVC
participant "ChatNodeComponent\n(the bubble you see)" as NODE
participant "LLM / proxy\nSSE stream" as NET

== 1. Create an empty assistant bubble ==
User -> UI : type question, hit send
UI -> LLM : streamAnswer(chatId, question, model)
LLM -> SVC : addNode(role=assistant, content="")
SVC --> NODE : Angular binds node()\nempty bubble appears
LLM -> SVC : startGeneration(answerNode.id)\n(generatingNodeId is set)
note over NODE
  Angular rookie note:
  The bubble is just a component
  whose input is node().
  When ChatService updates that node,
  Angular re-renders this component.
end note

== 2. Tokens arrive faster than we show them ==
LLM -> NET : askLlm(... stream: true)
loop each SSE chunk while the model is still writing
  NET --> LLM : chunk.content  (a few letters, not a full answer)
  LLM -> BUF : accContent += chunk\n(full text so far, not yet all visible)
  LLM -> PUMP : kickPump()
  note over BUF
    accContent  = everything received
    committed   = how far we are allowed
                  to show, paced by speed
    visible text = accContent[0 .. visibleEnd]
  end note
end

== 3. The pump reveals one unit at a time ==
loop requestAnimationFrame (~every screen refresh)
  PUMP -> PUMP : carry += dt * streamSpeed\n(seconds * chars/s or words/s)
  alt unit = chars/s
    PUMP -> BUF : committed += 1\n(endOfNextUnit = from + 1)
  else unit = words/s
    PUMP -> BUF : find next "word + space"\nin accContent after committed
    alt a complete word is already in the buffer
      PUMP -> BUF : committed jumps to end of that word
    else word is still incomplete\n(model has not sent the space yet)
      PUMP -> BUF : do nothing this frame\n(keep carry, wait for more SSE)
    end
  else streamSpeed = 0 (instant)
    PUMP -> BUF : committed = accContent.length\nshow everything received so far
  end

  PUMP -> SVC : paint()\nnode.content = accContent.slice(0, visibleEnd())
  SVC -> NODE : nodes() signal changes
  NODE -> NODE : effect() sees node().content
  NODE -> NODE : renderedHtml = markdown(content)
  NODE -> NODE : afterRenderEffect()\nfollowLive() if follow-streaming is on
  note over NODE
    afterRenderEffect waits until Angular
    has painted the new HTML.
    Then we scroll the nearest overflow
    parent so #streamEnd stays in view.
    That is "follow the stream".
  end note
end

== 4. Model finished — optional extra pacing ==
NET --> LLM : stream complete\n(result.content = full answer)
LLM -> BUF : accContent = result.content\nllmFinished = true

alt paceAfterComplete ON\nand streamSpeed > 0\nand committed still behind
  note over PUMP
    The HTTP stream is done,
    but the user still wants the
    same chars/s or words/s.
    drainReveal() keeps the pump
    running on the leftover buffer.
  end note
  loop until committed catches accContent
    PUMP -> BUF : reveal next char / word\n(last word is allowed now,\neven without a trailing space)
    PUMP -> SVC : paint() again
    SVC -> NODE : bubble grows, followLive()
  end
else paceAfterComplete OFF\nor instant speed\nor user aborted
  PUMP -> BUF : flushReveal()\ncommitted = full length\nshow the rest in one jump
  PUMP -> SVC : paint()
end

== 5. Persist and stop the spinner ==
LLM -> SVC : editAssistant(full text)\n(may create a new version id)
LLM -> SVC : stopGeneration()\ngeneratingNodeId = null
NODE -> NODE : isGenerating becomes false\nfollow effect stops

@enduml
